      "title": "Pope Leo votes in US midterms in first known political ballot for any pontiff",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/pope-leo-votes-us-midterms-first-political-ballot-pontiff",
      "description": "<p>US citizen Leo, who has clashed with Donald Trump over several issues, submits his vote by post in Chicago</p><p>Pope Leo has voted in the US midterm elections – the first time a sitting pontiff is known to have cast a ballot in any political election at any time in history.</p><p>Leo, who has clashed with the US president, Donald Trump, over several issues, submitted his vote by post in Chicago, where he was born, the Vatican said on Friday. Leo became the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/08/robert-francis-prevost-the-moderate-good-humoured-first-american-pope\">first American leader of the Catholic church</a> last year after the death of Pope Francis.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/30/pope-leo-votes-us-midterms-first-political-ballot-pontiff\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-30T16:01:21"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pope Leo calls for the disarmament of AI: ‘Machines are tools, not persons’",
      "link": "https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1023188/pope-leo-disarm-ai",
      "description": "Pope Leo XIV says AI systems should be \"disarmed,\" adding that humans \"have the responsibility to guide, change and, when necessary, reject its applications.\" In Friday's Papal Address, Pope Leo encourages United Nations member states to \"take concrete steps toward banning lethal autonomous weapons\" during their meeting in Geneva next month. The address reflects many [&#8230;]",
      "source_name": "The Verge All Posts",
      "published": "2026-10-30T14:58:06"
    }
